&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is located in Munich, Germany. TULIP is a hybrid work environment and we are in the office 3+ days/per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About TULIP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://tulip.co/"&gt;TULIP&lt;/a&gt; is the frontline operations platform that helps manufacturers digitize, connect and continuously improve how they run production, with AI at the core of the product. TULIP was founded out of the MIT Media Lab. It is headquartered in Boston, has offices in Munich, Tokyo, Tel Aviv, Budapest and Singapore, and has customer sites in more than 45 countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In January 2026, TULIP &lt;a href="https://tulip.co/press/tulip-secures-120m-series-d/"&gt;closed its $120M Series D&lt;/a&gt;, at a valuation of $1.3B. Leading global manufacturers run on TULIP, including VEKA, DMG Mori, Roche, AstraZeneca, Richemont, Saint-Gobain Aerospace and Mitsubishi Electric. We partner with NVIDIA, PwC, McKinsey, BCG and more than 160 technology partners worldwide. TULIP is part of the World Economic Forum's Global Innovator community, and our CEO, Dr. Natan Linder, co-chairs the Forum's Advanced Manufacturing Industry Governors Community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity in DACH for TULIP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DACH is the heart of global manufacturing. Germany is Europe's largest industrial economy and the birthplace of Industrie 4.0. Switzerland is a global centre for pharma, life sciences and precision manufacturing. Austria is a strong base in automotive, machinery, metals and semiconductors. The region is also home to many of the world's "Hidden Champions", mid-sized companies that lead global niche markets. Today, these companies face similar pressures: fewer skilled workers, rising quality and compliance demands, and the need to modernize existing plants without stopping production. TULIP gives their frontline teams an AI-native production system to meet those pressures and accelerate time-to-value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TULIP GmbH is a full operating entity and Munich is TULIP’s headquarters in Europe. The team covers sales, solutions engineering, pre-sales engineering, customer success, and R&amp;amp;D. Local customers trust our product in regulated, high-precision environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You're an engineering leader who cares about getting security-critical systems right and who wants to reach customers fast, not sit buried in a backlog. You think in specs and failure modes, you stay close to the code, and you're already using AI tooling to change how your team builds, not just how quickly they move. You'll take over a small, strong team and own how the world's most demanding manufacturers authenticate, provision, and govern access for their people and, increasingly, the AI agents acting on their behalf.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What skills do I need?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of software engineering experience, with direct involvement building and operating security-critical or identity/access systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of people management experience leading a software team, where you've hired, given constructive feedback, and grown engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on depth with OAuth 2.0, SAML 2.0, OIDC, and SCIM in enterprise environments — you understand the specs and their failure modes, not just the libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building multi-tenant systems where tenant isolation is a hard requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of IAM, secrets management, and access policy across AWS and Azure, including the tradeoffs when customers span both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of shipping clean, tested code and holding a team to the same standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active use of AI tooling in your own practice, with a point of view on how it changes the way teams build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field, or equivalent working experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture and roadmap for identity &amp;amp; access — SSO/SAML/OIDC federation, SCIM provisioning, multi-tenant account structures, and the authorization layer across Tulip's multi-cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Identity &amp;amp; Access in cross-functional architecture reviews and roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a small, high-caliber team — run regular 1:1s, set quality standards, give direct feedback, and develop engineers on security-critical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect operations where failures carry tangible stakes—from halted production lines to scrapped material and compliance risks. What you ship here has a direct impact on customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of AI tooling in how the team builds — code review, test generation, spec drafting, and agent loops — and share what works across engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and own difficult tradeoffs on IAM and access policy where tenant isolation and enterprise compliance are non-negotiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship work that reaches customers quickly and reliably, with operational excellence as the default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Collaborators&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security &amp;amp; Infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working At Tulip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know even great candidates experience imposter syndrome. Even if you don’t match every requirement, applying gives you the opportunity to be considered.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building a strong, diverse team that values hard work, families, and personal well-being. Benefits of working with us include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Direct impact on product and culture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Company equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Competitive benefits package including commuter benefits, learning and development stipend, team events, catered lunches 3 days a week&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Flexible work schedule and unlimited vacation policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;An inclusive, dog-friendly office with diverse and inspiring colleagues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Virtual and in-office global company events and happy hours&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class="content-conclusion"&gt;&lt;p class="p1"&gt;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="p1"&gt;Please note that we may use AI-based tools to support parts of our hiring process. All data processing is carried out in compliance with local data protection laws, ensuring all personal candidate information is handled securely and ethically.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;At Isar Aerospace, we are enabling affordable and flexible access to space. As Europe’s leading privately funded launch company, we are developing and operating launch vehicles that provide reliable access to orbit for commercial and institutional customers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;To support the continued development and operation of our launch systems, we are looking for a (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Senior) Flight Safety Engineer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt; to take ownership of flight safety engineering activities across vehicle development, licensing, and launch operations. In this role, you will drive the flight safety framework for our launch vehicles and act as a key interface between engineering, regulatory authorities, and launch range partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;As a (Senior) Flight Safety Engineer in the Mission and Launch operations team, you will work at the intersection of engineering, risk analysis and mission operations. In that frame, you will ensure that our launch systems meet the highest standards of safety, reliability, and regulatory compliance throughout the vehicle lifecycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class="TextRun SCXW114497174 BCX8" lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun CommentStart CommentHighlightPipeRest CommentHighlightRest SCXW114497174 BCX8"&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;&lt;span class="EOP CommentHighlightPipeRest SCXW114497174 BCX8" data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Own system-level flight safety engineering activities for launch vehicle development and operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Define, manage, and verify system requirements related to Range Safety Systems (RTS) and Flight Termination Systems (FTS), ensuring compliance with range and regulatory requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Support mission licensing activities and regulatory approvals, including preparation of safety analyses and compliance documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Coordinate with RAMS department to perform Functional Hazard Assessments (FHA), Failure Modes and Effects Analyses (FMEA), Failure Modes, Effects and Criticality Analyses (FMECA) to support the safety case.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Coordinate closely with Avionics, GNC, Flight Software, Propulsion, Structures, and Operations teams to ensure safety requirements are properly integrated into system design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Support the development, maintenance, and validation of debris and fragmentation models to assess flight safety risks and support mission approvals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Support flight safety analyses including trajectory risk assessments, casualty expectation calculations, and launch commit criteria development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Contribute to anomaly investigations, root cause analyses, and continuous improvement of flight safety methodologies and processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Support the evolution of Isar Aerospace's flight safety standards, tools, and engineering practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;&lt;span class="EOP CommentHighlightPipeRest SCXW114497174 BCX8" data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;Qualification Checklist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Master's degree or PhD in Aerospace Engineering, Systems Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related technical discipline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Minimum 5 years of professional experience in launch vehicle flight safety, system safety, reliability engineering, launch vehicle development, missile systems, or a comparable aerospace environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Strong experience with 14 CFR Part 450 and its application to launch licensing, hazard analysis, and public safety requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Demonstrated experience with FHA, FMEA, FMECA, fault tree analysis (FTA), reliability assessments, and safety case development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Experience working with RTS/FTS architectures, range safety requirements, and launch operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Ability to work effectively across multidisciplinary engineering organizations and influence technical decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills combined with a pragmatic engineering mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Excellent communication skills in English.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang="EN-US"&gt;Bonus Skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Experience working with commercial launch providers, defence programs, or space agencies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Familiarity with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;14 CFR part 450 (RCC319, 321 and 324) or equivalent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt; licensing processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Knowledge of Monte Carlo-based risk assessments, quantitative risk analysis and casualty expectation analyses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Basics of RF engineering and antenna systems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="auto"&gt;Experience developing or reviewing fragmentation, debris, and risk assessment models for aerospace applications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Experience supporting launch campaigns and mission readiness reviews.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Familiarity with ECSS, NASA, FAA, or range safety standards and practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast="none"&gt;Programming skills in Python, MATLAB, or similar analytical environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
